 3 v ⊗3 3 inside CP 2 .… \n\nFigures - uploaded by Elina Robeva\n\nAuthor content\n\nAll figure content in this area was uploaded by Elina Robeva\n\nContent may be subject to copyright.\n\nImage: ResearchGate Logo\n\nDiscover the world's research\n\n  * 25+ million members\n  * 160+ million publication pages\n  * 2.3+ billion citations\nJoin for free\n\nPublic Full-text 1\n\nPublisher Preview 1\n\nContent uploaded by Elina Robeva\n\nAuthor content\n\nAll content in this area was uploaded by Elina Robeva on Aug 11, 2015\n\nContent may be subject to copyright.\n\nOrthogonal Decomposition of Symmetric\n\nTensors\n\nElina Robeva\n\nUniversity of California, Berkeley\n\nAbstract\n\nA real symmetric tensor T is orthogonally decomposable (or odeco) if it can be\n\nwritten as T=λ 1 v⊗d\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOrthogonal Decomposition of Symmetric Tensors (https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.6685)\nciteturn2academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.1 years ago; Title: Orthogonal Decomposition of Symmetric TensorsAuthors: Elina Robeva ... A real symmetric tensor is orthogonally decomposable (or odeco) if it can be written as a linear combination of symmetric powers of $n$ vectors which form an orthonormal basis of $\\mathbb R^n$.Motivated by the spectral theorem for real symmetric matrices, we study the properties of odeco tensors.\nTitle: Orthogonal Decomposition of Symmetric Tensors\nAuthors: Elina Robeva\nDate: Tue Sep 23 18:14:17 2014\n\nA real symmetric tensor is orthogonally decomposable (or odeco) if it can be written as a linear combination of symmetric powers of $n$ vectors which form an orthonormal basis of $\\mathbb R^n$. Motivated by the spectral theorem for real symmetric matrices, we study the properties of odeco tensors. We give a formula for all of the eigenvectors of an odeco tensor. Moreover, we formulate a set of polynomial equations that vanish on the odeco variety and we conjecture that these polynomials 